      "Prioritise Google Ads when you need enquiries this month rather than next year: a new business, a new branch, a seasonal offer, or a service people search for with urgent intent — emergency repairs, same-day appointments, rentals. It also makes sense when your website is new and has not yet built any authority on Google, because paid search can generate demand while your organic presence is still developing.",
      "Google Ads also works well as a research tool. Running a focused campaign for a few months shows you which search terms actually convert into enquiries in your market — information that makes later SEO work much more targeted.",
      "## When SEO should come first",
      "SEO deserves priority when your category has high search demand and cost-per-click is expensive, when you sell something people research carefully before buying, or when you already have a healthy enquiry flow and want to reduce your long-term dependence on paid media.",
