      "Finally, look at internal linking: do the pages that matter most actually get linked to from elsewhere on the site, or are they orphaned several clicks deep in the navigation? None of this is a complete SEO strategy — but getting these fundamentals right is usually the highest-leverage first step before investing further in content or link building.",
      "## Technical checklist",
      "- Verify the site in Google Search Console and submit an XML sitemap.\n- Check the Page indexing report for pages that are excluded and why.\n- Confirm important pages don't carry a 'noindex' tag and aren't blocked in robots.txt.\n- Use one version of the domain (with or without www, always HTTPS) and redirect the others to it.\n- Set a canonical URL on every page, pointing to itself unless it's a deliberate duplicate.\n- Fix broken links and redirect retired URLs with permanent (301) redirects.\n- Check Core Web Vitals on mobile and compress oversized images.\n- Make sure important content is in the HTML, not only loaded by scripts after the page renders.",
      "## On-page checklist",
